e than 1,100 metres on the northern Meseta west of Madrid.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/avitus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/avitus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Avitus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Avitus was a Gallo-Roman aristocrat who became Western Roman emperor in 455 with the backing of the Visigothic king Theodoric II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/avongara"><span class="enc-name">Avongara</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Avongara are the aristocratic ruling clan of the Zande peoples of Central Africa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/avranches"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/avranches.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Avranches</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Avranches is a town in the Manche department of Normandy, north-western France, overlooking the bay of Mont-Saint-Michel.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/avranchin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/avranchin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Avranchin</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Avranchin is the historic district around Avranches in south-western Normandy, France, facing Mont-Saint-Michel across the bay.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/avungara"><span class="enc-name">Avungara</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Avungara are the ruling aristocratic clan of the Zande people of north-central Africa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/avvakum"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/avvakum.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" 