="enc-snip">The Ayarmaca were an Andean people whose lordship, centred north-west of Cusco in Peru, was one of the main rivals of the early Inca kingdom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ayas-cilicia"><span class="enc-name">Ayas (Cilicia)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ayas, the Laiazzo of Italian merchants, is a port on the Gulf of İskenderun in southern Turkey, now the town of Yumurtalık.</span></a></li></ul>
